/* Shardwild: MEGA KING, the true king the Hollow Guard (Morvane) served. Endgame dungeon art by Sprites.
 * Generated by king.py / minions.py / guards.py / tiles_mk.py / throne.py (export_js.py). NOT wired in;
 * Rotmg adds it only after Joshua says go.
 *
 * Visual tie to Morvane / Hollow UT: black plate + plum/purple cape + gold crown/trim + pink shard (#ff3f7a/#ffb8cc).
 * No serpent motifs.
 *
 * MEGAKING_FRAMES  - same {pal, frames:[idle, idle, wind-up, fire]} format as BOSS_FRAMES. 32x32 rows.
 *   megaking_p1  regal, armoured (crown on, chest gem sealed)
 *   megaking_p2  cracks + leaking shard light, crown on      (Rotmg: "phase 2 standing with his crown on")
 *   megaking_p3  chest plate broken, shard core showing
 *   megaking_p4  enraged: blazing core, crown floating + burning, big shards erupting, torn cape
 *                (Rotmg: "phase 4 cracked armour + core showing"). For a 3-phase fight use p1 -> p3 -> p4.
 *   Install like the other bosses: SPR.megaking_pN = mkAnim(frames, pal) with fit 1, swap e.d.spr / the anim on phase change.
 *   Suggested enemy def: scale:34*2.2/26 (same pixel size as every other boss -> ~98px tall), r:14.
 *   (Use scale:2.6 / ~88px if it crowds the phone view; Morvane is ~75px today.)
 *   'x' is the flash colour (#ffffff) used on the fire frame.
 *
 * MEGAKING_ENEMIES - same format as ENEMY_FRAMES.
 *   12x12 minions (install with the normal V25_FIT 0.667): shardguard, crystalcaster, royalhound, crownsentry, shardling
 *   16x16 mini-boss guards: kingsguard, shardherald. Suggested scale:1.2 (~22px) or elite base; fit 1.
 *
 * MEGAKING_TILES   - same structure as DUNGEON_TILES entries (pal, wallTop/2, wallLeft/Right, wallFace/2, wallDeep, edges,
 *   floors[4], details, props, rims). Same wall-selection rules as the dungeon set. Additions:
 *   wallBanner    - opaque wall-face variant (royal banner); use on ~1 in 6 north-wall faces of the throne hall.
 *   props.throneRC (R,C = 0..4) - 40x40 ruined crystal throne as 5x5 tiles, row R, column C. Floor shows through ('.').
 *   props.dais    - plain raised stone; rims.dais adds the gold lip on edges whose neighbour is not dais/throne.
 *   props.carpet / carpetEnd - royal runner; rims.carpet adds gold borders (carpetEnd counts as carpet; skip its S rim).
 *   props.pylon/pylon2 shard pylons, brazier, pillar, brokenPillar.
 *   props.rift/rift2 - shard-rift hazard; rims.rift like the other hazards.
 *   propsRaw      - the same transparent props WITHOUT floors[0] baked in, so brazier/pylon/throne can sit on dais or carpet.
 *
 * MEGAKING_KEY    - 8x8 rows for keyArt-style raw painting (mkRaw, no outline): SPR.keyMega = mkRaw(rows, pal).
 * MEGAKING_PORTAL - 8x8 rows for mkSprite (outlined), same as the other portalSpr rings: SPR.portalMega = mkSprite(rows, pal).
 *   Morvane drops the key (keySpr:'keyMega', portalSpr:'portalMega').
 */
